IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc21-part-17`

-- ccc21-tests-part-17.l4 -- tests for PART XVII (ss 530 to 534). Every expected value is written by hand from the text, beside the assertion, before the run.
-- Argument order is the GIVEN order of the function under test (see ccc21-part-17.l4).

§ `Tests -- section 530(1)`

-- 530(1): an accused whose language is official, who applied not later than the appearance at which the trial date is set: the judge shall grant. Order: official, applied, date applied, date of appearance.
#ASSERT `s 530(1) the judge, provincial court judge or justice shall grant the order` TRUE TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- on the day of the appearance: "not later than the time of the appearance" (boundary: same day)
#ASSERT `s 530(1) the judge, provincial court judge or justice shall grant the order` TRUE TRUE (Date 9 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the day before
#ASSERT `s 530(1) the judge, provincial court judge or justice shall grant the order` TRUE TRUE (Date 11 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the day after: later than the appearance (boundary)
#ASSERT `s 530(1) the judge, provincial court judge or justice shall grant the order` TRUE FALSE (Date 9 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no application: "On application by an accused"
#ASSERT `s 530(1) the judge, provincial court judge or justice shall grant the order` FALSE TRUE (Date 9 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING   -- language not official: (1) does not speak to it (subsection (2) does)
-- the content of the order
#ASSERT `s 530(1) the order directs trial before a justice or judge who speaks both official languages` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- circumstances warrant both
#ASSERT `s 530(1) the order directs trial before a justice or judge who speaks both official languages` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the official language of the accused only
#ASSERT `s 530(1) the order directs trial before a justice or judge who speaks both official languages` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no order granted: the text gives it no content
#ASSERT `s 530(1) the order directs trial before a justice or judge who speaks both official languages` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether the order is granted is not settled

§ `Tests -- section 530(2)`

-- 530(2): an accused whose language is not official: the court MAY grant. Order: language is official, applied, date applied, date of appearance.
#ASSERT `s 530(2) the judge, provincial court judge or justice may grant the order` FALSE TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- same day (boundary)
#ASSERT `s 530(2) the judge, provincial court judge or justice may grant the order` FALSE TRUE (Date 11 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- one day late
#ASSERT `s 530(2) the judge, provincial court judge or justice may grant the order` FALSE FALSE (Date 9 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no application
#ASSERT `s 530(2) the judge, provincial court judge or justice may grant the order` TRUE TRUE (Date 9 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING   -- language is official: subsection (1) is the one that speaks
#ASSERT `s 530(2) the order directs trial before a justice or judge who speaks both official languages` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530(2) the order directs trial before a justice or judge who speaks both official languages` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 530(2) the order directs trial before a justice or judge who speaks both official languages` (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 530(2) the order directs trial before a justice or judge who speaks both official languages` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- sections 530(3) to 530(6)`

#ASSERT `s 530(3) the judge, provincial court judge, judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice or justice of the peace shall ensure that the accused is advised of the right and of the time` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- first appearance before this judge
#ASSERT `s 530(3) the judge, provincial court judge, judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice or justice of the peace shall ensure that the accused is advised of the right and of the time` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not the first appearance: the duty is on the one "before whom an accused first appears"
-- 530(4): failed to apply, court satisfied it is in the best interests of justice, court does not speak the language. Order: failed to apply, satisfied, court speaks that language.
#ASSERT `s 530(4) the court may by order remand the accused to be tried before a justice or judge who speaks that language` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530(4) the court may by order remand the accused to be tried before a justice or judge who speaks that language` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the accused applied
#ASSERT `s 530(4) the court may by order remand the accused to be tried before a justice or judge who speaks that language` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not satisfied
#ASSERT `s 530(4) the court may by order remand the accused to be tried before a justice or judge who speaks that language` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the court speaks that language: "if it does not speak that language"
-- 530(5): variation either way, if the circumstances warrant.
#ASSERT `s 530(5) the court may vary the order to require the other` `s 530(5) one official language of Canada` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530(5) the court may vary the order to require the other` `s 530(5) both official languages of Canada` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "and vice versa"
#ASSERT `s 530(5) the court may vary the order to require the other` `s 530(5) both official languages of Canada` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- circumstances do not warrant
#ASSERT `s 530(5) the court may vary the order to require the other` `s 530(5) there is no order under section 530` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- there is no order to vary
-- 530(6): two or more accused tried together, each entitled, languages different.
#ASSERT `s 530(6) the facts may constitute circumstances that warrant an order for both official languages` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530(6) the facts may constitute circumstances that warrant an order for both official languages` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- one accused: a sufficient circumstance is missing, not a bar
#ASSERT `s 530(6) the facts may constitute circumstances that warrant an order for both official languages` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 530(6) the facts may constitute circumstances that warrant an order for both official languages` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the same official language

§ `Tests -- section 530.01`

-- 530.01(1)(a). Order: order granted, prosecutor is private, accused applied, a portion is in the other official language.
#ASSERT `s 530.01(1)(a) the prosecutor shall cause the portions to be translated` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530.01(1)(a) the prosecutor shall cause the portions to be translated` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no order under section 530
#ASSERT `s 530.01(1)(a) the prosecutor shall cause the portions to be translated` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a private prosecutor
#ASSERT `s 530.01(1)(a) the prosecutor shall cause the portions to be translated` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no application by the accused
#ASSERT `s 530.01(1)(a) the prosecutor shall cause the portions to be translated` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no portion is in the other official language: nothing to translate
-- 530.01(1)(b) follows the answer of (a).
#ASSERT `s 530.01(1)(b) the prosecutor shall provide the accused with a written copy of the translated text` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530.01(1)(b) the prosecutor shall provide the accused with a written copy of the translated text` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 530.01(1)(b) the prosecutor shall provide the accused with a written copy of the translated text` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- 530.01(2)
#ASSERT `s 530.01(2) the original version prevails` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530.01(2) the original version prevails` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no discrepancy: nothing to prevail over

§ `Tests -- section 530.1`

-- (a): order granted, stage.
#ASSERT `s 530.1(a) the accused and counsel have the right to use either official language for all purposes` TRUE `preliminary inquiry` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530.1(a) the accused and counsel have the right to use either official language for all purposes` TRUE `trial` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530.1(a) the accused and counsel have the right to use either official language for all purposes` FALSE `trial` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no order
#ASSERT `s 530.1(a) the accused and counsel have the right to use either official language for all purposes` TRUE `sentencing` EQUALS NOTHING   -- "during the preliminary inquiry and trial"
#ASSERT `s 530.1(b) the accused and counsel may use either official language in written pleadings or other documents` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530.1(b) the accused and counsel may use either official language in written pleadings or other documents` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 530.1(c) any witness may give evidence in either official language` TRUE `trial` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530.1(c) any witness may give evidence in either official language` TRUE `preliminary inquiry` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530.1(c) any witness may give evidence in either official language` FALSE `trial` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 530.1(c) any witness may give evidence in either official language` TRUE `appeal` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 530.1(c.1) the presiding justice or judge may authorize the prosecutor to examine or cross-examine a witness in the official language of the witness` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530.1(c.1) the presiding justice or judge may authorize the prosecutor to examine or cross-examine a witness in the official language of the witness` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- circumstances do not warrant
#ASSERT `s 530.1(c.1) the presiding justice or judge may authorize the prosecutor to examine or cross-examine a witness in the official language of the witness` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no order
#ASSERT `s 530.1(d) the accused has a right to have a justice presiding over the preliminary inquiry who speaks the official language of the accused or both official languages` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530.1(d) the accused has a right to have a justice presiding over the preliminary inquiry who speaks the official language of the accused or both official languages` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 530.1(e) the accused has a right to have a prosecutor who speaks the official language of the accused or both official languages` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530.1(e) the accused has a right to have a prosecutor who speaks the official language of the accused or both official languages` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "other than a private prosecutor"
#ASSERT `s 530.1(e) the accused has a right to have a prosecutor who speaks the official language of the accused or both official languages` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 530.1(f) the court shall make interpreters available` TRUE `trial` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530.1(f) the court shall make interpreters available` TRUE `preliminary inquiry` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530.1(f) the court shall make interpreters available` FALSE `trial` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 530.1(f) the court shall make interpreters available` TRUE `sentencing` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (g): order granted, stage, item.
#ASSERT `s 530.1(g) the record of proceedings shall include the item` TRUE `trial` `s 530.1(g)(i) a transcript of everything that was said, in the official language in which it was said` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530.1(g) the record of proceedings shall include the item` TRUE `trial` `s 530.1(g)(ii) a transcript of any interpretation into the other official language of what was said` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530.1(g) the record of proceedings shall include the item` TRUE `preliminary inquiry` `s 530.1(g)(iii) any documentary evidence tendered, in the official language in which it was tendered` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530.1(g) the record of proceedings shall include the item` TRUE `trial` `s 530.1(g) anything else` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the list is introduced by "shall include", not closed
#ASSERT `s 530.1(g) the record of proceedings shall include the item` FALSE `trial` `s 530.1(g)(i) a transcript of everything that was said, in the official language in which it was said` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 530.1(g) the record of proceedings shall include the item` TRUE `appeal` `s 530.1(g)(i) a transcript of everything that was said, in the official language in which it was said` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (h)
#ASSERT `s 530.1(h) the court shall make the written trial judgment available in the official language of the accused` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530.1(h) the court shall make the written trial judgment available in the official language of the accused` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 530.1(h) the court shall make the written trial judgment available in the official language of the accused` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not issued in writing

§ `Tests -- sections 530.2, 531, 532`

-- 530.2(1): both-languages order, stage, made at the start.
#ASSERT `s 530.2(1) the justice or judge presiding may make an order setting out the circumstances in which, and the extent to which, each official language may be used` TRUE `trial` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530.2(1) the justice or judge presiding may make an order setting out the circumstances in which, and the extent to which, each official language may be used` TRUE `preliminary inquiry` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530.2(1) the justice or judge presiding may make an order setting out the circumstances in which, and the extent to which, each official language may be used` FALSE `trial` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no order for both languages
#ASSERT `s 530.2(1) the justice or judge presiding may make an order setting out the circumstances in which, and the extent to which, each official language may be used` TRUE `sentencing` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 530.2(1) the justice or judge presiding may make an order setting out the circumstances in which, and the extent to which, each official language may be used` TRUE `trial` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not "at the start of the proceeding"
#ASSERT `s 530.2(2) the order shall, to the extent possible, respect the right of the accused to be tried in their official language` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530.2(2) the order shall, to the extent possible, respect the right of the accused to be tried in their official language` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 531: order made under 530, cannot be conveniently complied with, province, regulation governs.
#ASSERT `s 531 the court shall order that the trial be held in another territorial division in the same province` TRUE TRUE Ontario FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 531 the court shall order that the trial be held in another territorial division in the same province` TRUE TRUE `New Brunswick` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "except if that territorial division is in the Province of New Brunswick"
#ASSERT `s 531 the court shall order that the trial be held in another territorial division in the same province` TRUE FALSE Ontario FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the order can be conveniently complied with
#ASSERT `s 531 the court shall order that the trial be held in another territorial division in the same province` FALSE TRUE Ontario FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no order under section 530
#ASSERT `s 531 the court shall order that the trial be held in another territorial division in the same province` TRUE TRUE Ontario TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a regulation under section 533 governs: outside the sources
#ASSERT `s 531 the court shall order that the trial be held in another territorial division in the same province` TRUE TRUE Yukon FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a territory: "the same province"
#ASSERT `s 531 the court shall order that the trial be held in another territorial division in the same province` TRUE TRUE `British Columbia` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 532: afforded by a provincial law, in force, relates to language, inconsistent.
#ASSERT `s 532 this Part and the Official Languages Act do not derogate from the right` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 532 this Part and the Official Languages Act do not derogate from the right` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- inconsistent: the section does not speak to it
#ASSERT `s 532 this Part and the Official Languages Act do not derogate from the right` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 532 this Part and the Official Languages Act do not derogate from the right` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 532 this Part and the Official Languages Act do not derogate from the right` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 534: the text shows the section repealed
#ASSERT `s 534 repealed` EQUALS "534 [Repealed, 1997, c. 18, s. 63]"

§ `Trace -- section 530.01(1): translate, then give a copy`

-- expected: FULFILLED (both steps taken in order)
#TRACE `s 530.01(1) the prosecutor must have the portions translated and then give the accused a written copy` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 530.01(1) causes the portions to be translated` AT 1
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 530.01(1) provides the accused with a written copy of the translated text` AT 2
